Lady Elowen and the Great Festival Supply Quest :

In the bright kingdom of Larkhill, the castle bell rang once, twice, three times—clear as a silver spoon tapping a cup. It was the morning signal for all good folk to begin their work.

Lady Elowen, the bravest knight in the king’s service, was already dressed and ready before the last ring faded. Her armor shone like a polished kettle, and her cloak was as red as a ripe apple.

Elowen was famous for her quick thinking, her kindness, and her courage. In the Great Hall, King Aldren waited with a map.

“Lady Elowen,” he said, “our Festival of Lanterns is near, but our storehouse is low. We need bread, beans, apples, cheese, and oats. Will you gather these supplies?”

Elowen placed her hand on her heart. “Gladly, Your Majesty.”

With her loyal pony, Sir Puddles, she set off on her quest.

She rode through green fields and reached River Bramble, only to find the bridge missing. A ferryman offered to take her across in exchange for a joke. Elowen told a clever joke, and the ferryman laughed, happily ferrying her across.

On the other side, she found that village signs were mixed up, causing confusion among the villagers. Apples were in Beanmeadow, beans were in Oatendale, and oats were in the wrong place.

Elowen gathered the villagers and helped organize them. She created a plan to return supplies to their proper locations and worked with the sign painter to fix the signs.

With teamwork and smart thinking, everything was sorted out.

Elowen collected all the needed supplies and returned to the castle just in time.

The king praised her courage and wisdom. The cooks cheered, and the festival preparations began.

Elowen smiled, knowing that helping others was the greatest kind of bravery.
